deadlines:
  title: When eInvoicing Becomes Mandatory
  lead: >-
    The UAE Ministry of Finance is bringing businesses into the eInvoicing system in phases. A PDF or
    paper invoice will no longer count once your phase starts.
  list:
    - date: 1 January 2027
      who: Businesses with revenue of AED 50 million or more
      what: eInvoicing becomes mandatory.
    - date: 31 March 2027
      who: All other businesses and government entities
      what: Deadline to appoint an Accredited Service Provider.
    - date: 1 July 2027
      who: Businesses with revenue below AED 50 million
      what: eInvoicing becomes mandatory.
    - date: 1 October 2027
      who: Government entities
      what: eInvoicing becomes mandatory.
  note: >-
    Dates are those set by Ministerial Decision No. 244 of 2025 and its amendments. Confirm the ones
    that apply to you with the <a href="https://mof.gov.ae">Ministry of Finance</a>.
